  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200B;Providing Lifesaving Humanitarian Assistance in Collective Centers in Zakarpattia Oblast in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 24 February 2022, the Russian Federation launched a broad military offensive against Ukraine, resulting in the displacement of over 7.1 million people as of 30 May. The majority of internally displaced persons (IDPs) are currently residing in Western Ukraine, including Zakarpattia Oblast. The overall scale and unpredictability of the situation requires immediate humanitarian assistance for the most vulnerable displaced and conflict-affected communities. Through various assessments, IOM has identified the need to improve living conditions in collective centres in Zakarpattia Oblast, especially in light of the upcoming winter season. Through this project, IOM aims to improve living conditions for IDPs in collective centres by carrying out light repairs and upgrades to collective centres to prepare them for harsh winter conditions, as well as repairing and maintaining water and sanitation facilities in collective centres. IOM is also ensuring that IDPs in collective centres are provided with essential items and services, including through referral to service providers.</narrative>
  </description>
